0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-124123"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066119/assets/8417d2d62e9213ec3f92108495107fc982dc399e52cca8982e01516457f5692a.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{2y}{x}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-right quarter of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNote that we can write the equation of our ellipse in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2$ and $3,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{2y}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124123/selection/ma-v1/211ab7991850e1954e534eeea7d324db0b71ec839c52d11ae479a94435d2ff0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa" :answer/id #uuid "81ff744f-5e4e-5050-874f-7a16e3f2eb69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" :answer/id #uuid "10bf22ff-1d37-5615-a0d2-3b6919650d58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "174d65c4-9616-5be0-9eb4-1d38c85da8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection/fba918d936ec8a8857b6fc6984940ee860d3d39fbe77c995f1d64ac962ebb2cd" :answer/id #uuid "d70814cc-b73e-5e5a-b2d7-ce208dfea8ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "d8854a1a-391d-581d-9781-7be91bc86ebd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7af62dda-d68c-5c00-bb57-3f8bec4f58e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124175/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124175/selection/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa" "q-124175/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" "q-124175/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-124175/selection/fba918d936ec8a8857b6fc6984940ee860d3d39fbe77c995f1d64ac962ebb2cd" "q-124175/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124175" :question/id #uuid "7e7fe208-545d-517b-a221-dc0140c73316" :question/math-academy-id "q-124175" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066119/assets/ab95b870025708090e40cbd7645072e8f4453cf50047b2a00036a30171c81994.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}(\\sqrt{x-1}+y)\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(1,2)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(1,2)$ and $(2,1).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(1+t(2-1)),\\,(2+t(1-2))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+t,\\,2-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x-1}+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{(1+t)-1}+2-t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}-t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{t}-t+2)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{1/2}-t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+2t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+2)-(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124175/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "26c8ffe3-42c4-59aa-9857-153eae63aa45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "23187d9f-9f5f-58d0-af79-ea3d7b022e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "426a5f6d-092e-56b4-9231-cae40de78bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "f8c54783-6256-59c1-a737-4ed96f0d6223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "459e44d2-36bd-5a8b-9b8b-b0930d6174d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "917323fc-71c2-5089-8ea2-2a988a2dcb16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124177/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-124177/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" "q-124177/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-124177/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-124177/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-124177/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124177" :question/id #uuid "4a81f809-64bd-5578-8059-0ccd53e29b69" :question/math-academy-id "q-124177" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066119/assets/272b0afabca579f65cbaa7949fd1be70427ff0fd860eb953207bbc8eda7b6e9c.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{3x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-left quarter of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $3$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x}{y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{3(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =-9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-9[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-9(0-1) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124177/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b45822-868e-51bb-b551-345739e9ca44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124177"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection/594afd4a905b730933d328759e75d8e37e933cab8ede505fc872f3df678601d4" :answer/id #uuid "04e05201-ffe4-5f35-aac1-9d6a5ba42ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection/e753dd9b6d5a42cdba106a50e9822748caa1eab57381f1c7824af1054f30d36f" :answer/id #uuid "cfbc66d3-b386-518b-bd8b-28c4021e30d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection/7019e9b1c75e72a49913abeb49ae7d626e0e0d59948bc42baf67eaed963fb9f6" :answer/id #uuid "939cf0eb-ec19-5fb5-ab90-1bb83ecba1c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection/a17d7e2b62489cffa356af5cc5a88918db59640f6f983b3dfb1985c2c4679e42" :answer/id #uuid "6f192825-2bb6-52b4-a5fa-a4b1515a7b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection/7d89a3a1e0d3117a8596db8eade9a501dc94efacbcf596420f5d5be1190b32b9" :answer/id #uuid "13ba3a31-419e-55d6-92d7-e99b3f85e7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4677ee8-4e7a-5d3f-ae70-1441a85109bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124277/selection/594afd4a905b730933d328759e75d8e37e933cab8ede505fc872f3df678601d4" :answer-field/choices ["q-124277/selection/594afd4a905b730933d328759e75d8e37e933cab8ede505fc872f3df678601d4" "q-124277/selection/e753dd9b6d5a42cdba106a50e9822748caa1eab57381f1c7824af1054f30d36f" "q-124277/selection/7019e9b1c75e72a49913abeb49ae7d626e0e0d59948bc42baf67eaed963fb9f6" "q-124277/selection/a17d7e2b62489cffa356af5cc5a88918db59640f6f983b3dfb1985c2c4679e42" "q-124277/selection/7d89a3a1e0d3117a8596db8eade9a501dc94efacbcf596420f5d5be1190b32b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124277" :question/id #uuid "48afea1b-7419-5b27-97ac-ca8861895f05" :question/math-academy-id "q-124277" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066119/assets/f532544febd248846eede65941f4617d325d0f91fec291d2679ba28abb2fb8fc.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along a circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(-2,0)$ to the point $(0,-2),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124277/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection/9c00ef9b9f2dcbd0d8c5e574b028dd1d27020bffddf071db5bb169d61f32c92f" :answer/id #uuid "aa2c5158-aecb-5d83-8ba6-7a605e537d07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection/72319dc5e2207ba2766c7f66fbd70bae96cf5ed10f12de0737a3db103c9cbccc" :answer/id #uuid "c40beb16-89b7-51ca-bace-c345e21e0578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection/a04283d2985d61be8e1e3bbbff70e52ac14e21ad0f13286d34e8d874eafcf030" :answer/id #uuid "eaa91ebe-7d0a-54b8-a8da-621d0f322138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection/7db0e2eba63ae0ac052a98054a956006bf8f975d76adf842622fd725767df0ab" :answer/id #uuid "4297bdff-2272-5ebf-a9d9-dc25fb6ff329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection/14747b36a13dea4ac2b02e6b010d12e08dcb2722239d735dd51496bb7a0b3c73" :answer/id #uuid "59d0ef42-372b-5472-83d5-d8376b1f2d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3824a7d0-61b3-5e7b-b124-9d6e170ff34f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124287/selection/9c00ef9b9f2dcbd0d8c5e574b028dd1d27020bffddf071db5bb169d61f32c92f" :answer-field/choices ["q-124287/selection/9c00ef9b9f2dcbd0d8c5e574b028dd1d27020bffddf071db5bb169d61f32c92f" "q-124287/selection/72319dc5e2207ba2766c7f66fbd70bae96cf5ed10f12de0737a3db103c9cbccc" "q-124287/selection/a04283d2985d61be8e1e3bbbff70e52ac14e21ad0f13286d34e8d874eafcf030" "q-124287/selection/7db0e2eba63ae0ac052a98054a956006bf8f975d76adf842622fd725767df0ab" "q-124287/selection/14747b36a13dea4ac2b02e6b010d12e08dcb2722239d735dd51496bb7a0b3c73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124287" :question/id #uuid "26a386e8-4f71-5301-b2d4-aba31281f90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124287" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066119/assets/69a10b5524670d31cfc9f2982e37d58a5ee9ca39fe49f35b9dace011275a635a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(9-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along three-quarters of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(1,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =9-(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =9-9{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =9(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =9{cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }9{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =27{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124287/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0712bb6-c0f8-5551-8362-ae23629aa618"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124287"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
